<section #sec:named | Convergence title>

The first section is authored as a named `<section>` tag.

<# #sec:sigil | Convergence title #>

The second section is authored as a sigil `<#>` tag with the same title.

# Convergence title

The third section is authored as a bare markdown `#` heading with the same
title (no id — the bare-markdown form has no surface for one).

After the normalize-to-canonical gate runs, all three sections must produce
the structurally identical Layer 1 `<section>` node — same tagname, same
section-title shape, same title text — modulo the absence of an id on the
bare-markdown form. This is the convergence proof the section-form ladder
closure depends on.
